# astrobot-lab current commands: Phase 5 test workflow

This is the short reference for running the current Lunaryard stack with the
Phase 5 GUI. The active robot namespace is `/astrobot_0`; ROS uses
`ROS_DOMAIN_ID=177`; Foxglove bridge is `ws://127.0.0.1:8765`; GUI backend is
`http://127.0.0.1:8080`; React dev UI is `http://127.0.0.1:5173`.

## 0. Bring up Lunaryard

Headless, rocks enabled, default seed:

```bash
OMNILRS_ROCKS_ENABLED=true \
OMNILRS_GT_TF_ENABLED=false \
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml up -d --build --force-recreate
```

Visible Isaac Sim window:

```bash
xhost +local:root
DISPLAY=${DISPLAY:-:0} \
OMNILRS_HEADLESS=false \
OMNILRS_ROCKS_ENABLED=true \
OMNILRS_GT_TF_ENABLED=false \
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml up -d --build --force-recreate
```

Useful seed/resource overrides:

```bash
DISPLAY=${DISPLAY:-:0} \
OMNILRS_HEADLESS=false \
OMNILRS_ENVIRONMENT_SEED=411 \
OMNILRS_RESOURCE_MODE=random \
OMNILRS_RESOURCE_SEED=411 \
OMNILRS_ROCKS_ENABLED=true \
OMNILRS_GT_TF_ENABLED=false \
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml up -d --force-recreate
```

Open a dev shell:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash
```

## 1. Start Foxglove bridge

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec -d astrobot-dev bash -lc 'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && exec ros2 launch foxglove_bridge foxglove_bridge_launch.xml address:=0.0.0.0 port:=8765'
```

Connect Foxglove Desktop or Web to:

```text
ws://127.0.0.1:8765
```

Remote tunnel, if needed:

```bash
ssh -L 8765:127.0.0.1:8765 -L 8080:127.0.0.1:8080 -L 5173:127.0.0.1:5173 <user>@<remote-host>
```

Foxglove fixed frame: `map`

Core topics:

```text
/astrobot_0/slam/pose_corrected
/astrobot_0/slam/bev_costmap
/astrobot_0/slam/prob_voxel_map
/astrobot_0/slam/aligned_points_corrected
/astrobot_0/exploration/status
/astrobot_0/exploration/events
/astrobot_0/exploration/selected_goal
/astrobot_0/exploration/frontiers
/astrobot_0/diagnostics
/astrobot_0/plan
/astrobot_0/cmd_vel
/astrobot_0/lidar_0/pointcloud/raw
/astrobot_0/lidar_0/pointcloud/filtered
/astrobot_0/imu
/gt/map
/gt/base_link_pose
/gt/resource_maps/water
```

`/gt/*` is for UI/debug/evaluation, except the synthetic RTK/beacon path uses
`/gt/base_link_pose` to generate `/rtk/pose` when `start_synthetic_rtk:=true`.

## 2. Launch a Phase 5 mission stack

These launches start Phase 3 nav + Phase 4 mission logic. Run one at a time.

Sample-return mission:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && cd /workspace/astrobot-lab/astrobot-lab && source install/setup.bash && ros2 launch astrobot_launch phase4_exploration.launch.py mission_mode:=sample_return sample_success_threshold:=0.75 home_radius_m:=8.0 max_duration_sec:=1200.0'
```

Explore-radius mission:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && cd /workspace/astrobot-lab/astrobot-lab && source install/setup.bash && ros2 launch astrobot_launch phase4_exploration.launch.py mission_mode:=explore_radius coverage_goal_fraction:=0.70 home_radius_m:=8.0 mission_cell_size_m:=2.0 max_goal_distance_m:=8.0 max_duration_sec:=1200.0'
```

Teleop-click mission:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && cd /workspace/astrobot-lab/astrobot-lab && source install/setup.bash && ros2 launch astrobot_launch phase4_exploration.launch.py mission_mode:=teleop_click home_radius_m:=8.0 max_duration_sec:=3600.0'
```

## 3. Launch the Phase 5 GUI backend

In another terminal:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && cd /workspace/astrobot-lab/astrobot-lab && source install/setup.bash && ros2 launch astrobot_launch phase5_gui.launch.py'
```

Backend checks:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/health
curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/state | jq '.robots[0], .mission'
```

Do not open `http://127.0.0.1:8080/` as the UI page. It is API-only, so the
root path returning `{"detail":"Not Found"}` is normal.

## 4. Run the React GUI

Run locally on the host:

```bash
cd ui/astrobot-console
npm run dev -- --host 127.0.0.1
```

Open:

```text
http://127.0.0.1:5173
```

The Vite dev server proxies `/api` and `/ws` to the backend on
`127.0.0.1:8080`.

Teleop-click usage:

```text
1. Launch mission_mode:=teleop_click.
2. Launch phase5_gui.launch.py.
3. Open http://127.0.0.1:5173.
4. Enable "Teleop click" on the BEV panel.
5. Click a reachable point on the obstacle map.
```

Direct teleop API test:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/robots/astrobot_0/teleop_goal \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"x": 4.0, "y": 2.0, "yaw": 0.0, "frame_id": "map"}'
```

## 5. Quick ROS checks

List high-value topics:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && ros2 topic list | sort | grep -E "astrobot_0/(slam|exploration|diagnostics|resource|cmd_vel|plan|imu|lidar)|/gt/|/rtk"'
```

Watch mission status:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && ros2 topic echo /astrobot_0/exploration/status'
```

Watch diagnostics:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && ros2 topic echo /astrobot_0/diagnostics'
```

Manual Nav2 goal, if exploration is not running:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml exec astrobot-dev bash -lc \
  'source /etc/ros_setup.sh && ros2 action send_goal /astrobot_0/navigate_to_pose nav2_msgs/action/NavigateToPose "{pose: {header: {frame_id: map}, pose: {position: {x: 4.0, y: 2.0, z: 0.0}, orientation: {w: 1.0}}}}"'
```

## 6. Stop

Stop everything:

```bash
docker compose -f docker-compose.lunaryard.yml down
```

Hard cleanup of stopped containers only:

```bash
docker container prune
```
